   },
   {
    "quote": "Lithuanian developer Inion Software has launched a virtual power plant (VPP) platform for storage and distributed energy assets. The company has dual aims: it is currently operational in Lithuania’s balancing market and expanding, while it also has a goal of rolling its VPP platform out as a white-label offering for energy companies and aggregators under their own brands.",
    "url": "https://www.ess-news.com/2026/09/14/inion-software-launches-vpp-platform-and-white-label-offer-for-batteries-and-renewable-assets/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "White-label",
    "url": "https://www.ess-news.com/2026/09/14/inion-software-launches-vpp-platform-and-white-label-offer-for-batteries-and-renewable-assets/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "“We can offer the VPP as a white-label product,” said Šarūnas Stanaitis, CEO of Inion Software. “One of our strengths is integrating the hardware with the platform, which can be a difficult part of VPP deployment. Expanding this product outside Lithuania is one of our targets.”",
    "url": "https://www.ess-news.com/2026/09/14/inion-software-launches-vpp-platform-and-white-label-offer-for-batteries-and-renewable-assets/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Cross-border expansion of European VPP software is often slowed by local regulations and fragmented TSO frameworks, limiting expansion prospects for companies that interact with grids. The company notes, as a white-label option, the architecture pairs standard hardware at the energy sites with Inion’s software to handle the equipment connection and control logic.",
    "url": "https://www.ess-news.com/2026/09/14/inion-software-launches-vpp-platform-and-white-label-offer-for-batteries-and-renewable-assets/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
